# HG changeset patch
# User Betterbird <betterbird@betterbird.eu> and DeepSeek
# Date 1790109850 -7200
# Parent  29e082d49e740c2d48650f1822e0f3cbc83b6143
NNN35 - Keep Tags folder mode views, counts and caches up to date when tags change.

Issues fixed:
https://github.com/Betterbird/thunderbird-patches/issues/581
https://github.com/Betterbird/thunderbird-patches/issues/603
https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1954441

Note that Betterbird caches virtual folders completely, see:
1923520-fix-caching-for-virtual-folders.patch
So parts of this patch only apply to Betterbird. Those are clearly marked.

When a tag was added to or removed from a message, an open tag folder
view kept showing messages which no longer matched, the message counts
next to the tags in the folder pane were only refreshed when the tag
folder was opened, and the cached search results were left stale, so
that reopening the folder restored an outdated view.

- nsMsgXFVirtualFolderDBView::OnHdrPropertyChanged() now handles keyword
  (tag) changes: newly matching messages are added to the view,
  no-longer-matching messages are removed, the cached search results of
  the folder the message lives in are corrected via
  nsMsgDatabase::UpdateHdrInCache(), and the search folder's message and
  unread counts are updated from the view state. While extra search
  terms are active the cache is invalidated instead.
- SmartMailboxUtils listens for keyword changes and adjusts the tag
  folder counts and cached search results when the folder is not
  displayed in any 3-pane window.
- Renaming a tag in the settings is now also reflected in the Tags
  folder pane mode when that mode isn't currently active (bug 1954441).

Test checklist: tag/untag from a tag view (message disappears/appears instantly);
tag from Inbox and watch the Tags pane counter; rename a tag while Tags mode is off, then enable it.

